what The demos guard's roster holds one page and my own card asks whether a second joins on a hand's reading or by an entry rule a page can meet itself. Measured on docs-geode/tutorials/the-first-hour.md: 11 sh fences, 2 genuine answered pairs, and the pairing rule glues a command to the nearest following plain fence across arbitrary prose -- so vendor/zig-toolchain/zig version pairs with the already=yes block that answers fetch-toolchain five lines and a paragraph later. The demos page never exposed it because its answers sit close. Add a third marker, shown, above an sh block a page offers a reader without answering, which stops both the run and the pairing; add --pairs, which prints what a page would run and exits without running it, so a hand can read a candidate page before admitting it; then join the first hour with 9 shown blocks and 2 checked pairs.
