what Patchouli's standing ask on the card -- the QA report card grades a Rishi witness head at Door while Gauge's own setting table names a witness header Meter, and 19 of 40 SAMPLED tools/*_witness.rish read below B. The card already computes the whole answer per file and reports it: program_genre, program_genre_meter, meter_shadow and meter_shadow_moves are printed on every program and scored by nothing. What is missing is a COUNT. Build a census over the 2,910 tracked files the genre reading names -- 2,180 _witness, 394 _scan, 336 _control -- reading each file's Door composite and its Meter shadow, and printing per genre: below-B at Door, below-B at Meter, how many cross the door, and the mean move. A sample sizes a class; only a count names its shapes, and the ask cannot be ruled red, ratchet or card-that-says-so without one.
